WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.569 --> 00:00:06.610
Well, I'm honored to be
lighting bolt number one.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.310
My name is Jonathan
Reuing-Scherer.

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.120
I teach statistics here at Yale.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.620
I'm going to give
a quick discussion

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.780
about the way you use
video capture that's

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:14.652
built into Canvas.

00:00:14.652 --> 00:00:16.860
So the first one I'm to talk
about is called Panopto.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.910
I am not a Panopto
expert, nor do I

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.370
get paid by them to tell this.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.419
So just ask, and I'll
tell you straight

00:00:22.419 --> 00:00:24.702
up what my experience is.

00:00:24.702 --> 00:00:26.910
If you go to Panopto's
website, what they'll tell you

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.360
that is that it's the
easiest way to manage,

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.280
live stream, record,
and share videos

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.465
across your organization.

00:00:31.465 --> 00:00:33.340
And so the deal is it's
actually sort of part

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.250
hardware, part software,
part web-based interface.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:40.330
And so there are a number
of classrooms around here

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:43.030
at Yale now that have basically
a permanent built-in camera.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:44.655
And in addition to
the built-in camera,

00:00:44.655 --> 00:00:46.210
there's this box,
which is basically

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:48.100
it's like a computer
with a big hard drive.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.810
And the computer with
the big hard drive

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:51.575
is then tied in not
only to the camera,

00:00:51.575 --> 00:00:53.950
but also to whatever is being
presented in the classroom.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.840
So essentially, it's a
box that will capture

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.597
what's the camera,
whatever mic you're

00:00:57.597 --> 00:00:59.180
wearing in the
classroom, and whatever

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.280
is going up on the screen.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:03.160
It sort of automatically
captures all of those things.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.960
Now, it's also
software that you don't

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.010
have to have on your computer--

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:07.634
I do on mine-- which
means you can also

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.700
use it to do a quick
video capture of yourself

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:11.770
just through your own camera.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:14.290
So if you wanted to respond to
questions that students posed

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:16.270
online, or like, I got
the feeling in class

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:17.561
that you didn't get this today.

00:01:17.561 --> 00:01:19.510
Here's three
minutes of response.

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:22.480
Very easy then to
upload onto Canvas.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.590
And so it's also, then, a
web-based interface, which

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:27.840
is part of what I really like.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.340
It's built-in to Canvas,
which is it's a great way

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.580
to grab the videos automatically
from those specialized

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:34.480
classrooms.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:37.060
Or you can upload your own
videos that you make yourself.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.700
I often use a program called
Camtasia, which is frankly,

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:41.920
a great video editing
software program

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:44.170
that I use for making
high quality content

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.300
videos that I use.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.552
But Panopto is a great
way to organize those.

00:01:48.552 --> 00:01:50.510
It's also a great way
just to watch the videos.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.343
So it's also the interface
that students use

00:01:52.343 --> 00:01:54.420
to experience video capture.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.980
And say, it's also John
Harford-- if he's not here,

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.980
find him, because he's the
dude, walking right out there,

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:01.630
who's one of our
local Panopto experts.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:05.740
And he's been awesome for
helping me integrate this.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:08.920
So I used Panopto video
capture in three classes

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.000
over the last 12 months.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.460
One of them is a huge class,
about 250 students, STAT 10x.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:16.061
It's basically intro stats,
for mostly undergrads.

00:02:16.061 --> 00:02:17.560
I also have, then,
a flipped version

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:19.660
of intro stats, which
is mostly grad students,

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:20.940
but a few undergrads.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.450
This particular
class, actually, I

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:27.430
use that program can Camtasia
to make 50 high quality content

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:29.980
videos that students
watch before class.

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:33.040
And then, the class time is
used to run examples and answer

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:33.737
questions.

00:02:33.737 --> 00:02:35.320
Then also, this
semester, I'm teaching

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:36.500
multivariate statistics.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.100
This is an upper level, advanced
class for grad students.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.360
There's about 110 of them.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:43.000
And in this class,
it's also a live class.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.550
So both the huge class, and
then, this multi-variate class

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:46.720
are classes I teach live.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:49.690
I stand up, I give a lecture,
students show the usual time.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:53.170
But the camera also pops on
automatically for each class.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:56.530
And so there's a video capture
of the lecture as well.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:02.350
So what I used in this STAT
10x class in multi-variate--

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:04.774
so I captured the videos,
they showed up automatically.

00:03:04.774 --> 00:03:06.940
One of the things that's
great about the integration

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:10.030
of Panopto into Canvas is
that, literally, in week one,

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:12.640
I spent 20 minutes and
preprogrammed every time

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.830
that the camera needed
to show up or turn on

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:15.972
in a particular classroom.

00:03:15.972 --> 00:03:17.680
And that was the last
I thought about it.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:18.970
So otherwise, I just
show up in class.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:20.500
I plug-in my laptop,
as I always do,

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.960
and the recording
happens automatically.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:23.890
It streams live.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:26.380
It's about 40-second
delay is what [INAUDIBLE].

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:28.900
But I hear they're trying
to get it down to 20, or so.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.790
But it also, then,
automatically records it.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:34.480
And so students, then, can go
on after the fact and watch

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.310
videos.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.870
For my intro class,
Panopto is also

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:39.890
good as a video
organizational tool.

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:42.460
So as I said, I've produced
these content videos

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:43.567
for the flipped version.

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:45.400
But after a couple of
years, I was like, ah,

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:46.840
everyone who's in
the intro class

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:48.730
might as well have access
to those if they like them.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:50.860
So it's also a great way
just to kind of organize

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:53.420
what the videos look like.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.570
So this is more about
how do I tend to teach.

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:58.000
So my experience
with intro stats

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.790
is I'm trying to create
a multitude of ways

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:03.640
that people can learn--
sort of a stat smorgasbord.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:07.000
And so any class I teach,
there's like 1,000 slides.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:07.810
Big font.

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:09.984
They're sort of like that size.

00:04:09.984 --> 00:04:10.900
So they can use those.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.970
I release them in four
batches, so they're always

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:16.060
three weeks ahead, if
they want to read ahead.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:17.999
They can come to class
where I'll lecture,

00:04:17.999 --> 00:04:18.790
as I would usually.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.456
And I'm happy to
answer their questions.

00:04:20.456 --> 00:04:22.764
There's the video capture
of what happens live.

00:04:22.764 --> 00:04:24.430
And then, for the
intro classes, there's

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.430
this kind of topic videos

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:30.160
So the deal is students can
decide to come to class if they

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.562
want, but they don't have to.

00:04:31.562 --> 00:04:33.520
So if they'd rather just
stay home in their PJs

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:36.520
and watch the videos, that
is totally fine with me.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:38.170
Or they can watch the PDF files.

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:40.880
Or they can do any
combination of those things.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.440
And my experience is that
students do all of those.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:47.200
Some of them have a
particular modality they like.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.450
Many of them use more
than one, depending

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:52.210
on what's going on in their
lives and also the topic

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:54.100
that we're discussing.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.800
So for those of you who
might be thinking like, gosh,

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:00.127
if I video capture my class,
no one will ever show up again.

00:05:00.127 --> 00:05:01.960
So that was certainly--
you know, I thought,

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:04.335
what if I show up and there's
just me and the video camera?

00:05:04.335 --> 00:05:04.835
[LAUGHTER]

00:05:04.835 --> 00:05:07.430
So what I discovered is that,
in the large intro class,

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:09.530
only about 25% of
students decided

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.090
to exclusively watch the video.

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:12.631
So they just stayed
at home, and that

00:05:12.631 --> 00:05:14.826
was the only way they wanted
to use the information.

00:05:14.826 --> 00:05:17.200
It's been a larger percentage
in the multi-variate class.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:20.896
So about 35% to 40% of students
decide to stay at home.

00:05:20.896 --> 00:05:21.770
But it's interesting.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:24.264
Even of the people
who show up in class--

00:05:24.264 --> 00:05:26.180
every semester, I'll
say, quick show of hands.

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:27.764
Who's watched the
video at least once?

00:05:27.764 --> 00:05:29.596
Now, students don't
like to raise their hand

00:05:29.596 --> 00:05:30.560
under any circumstance.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:34.890
And still, 95% of
hands go up and say,

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:37.280
we used it at least once.

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:39.170
Here are the reasons
that they talked about

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:41.164
for wanting to use the videos.

00:05:41.164 --> 00:05:42.830
They had another class
at the same time.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:45.500
They had to miss for
illness, et cetera.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:48.620
Or they might just use the
video to review other topics.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:52.550
So what I really want
to do now is just

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:55.190
sort of go show you
what this looks like.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:59.690
So if you are in Canvas,
the way that this looks here

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:02.272
is that there's something
called Media Library here.

00:06:02.272 --> 00:06:03.980
And so all of the
videos that I recorded,

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:05.840
they just show up like that.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.569
And so to watch a
video then, this

00:06:07.569 --> 00:06:09.860
is sort of what it actually
looks like, if you actually

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:11.400
are watching a video.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.880
So students, then, if
they're watching video,

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:15.692
they get the screen
capture over here.

00:06:15.692 --> 00:06:16.900
Or if they want to watch me--

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:18.233
I don't know who would want to--

00:06:18.233 --> 00:06:20.090
but they can watch
me there, as well.

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:22.970
The audio was good, as long
as you have a good mic on,

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:23.780
as well.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:26.599
If you're using Camtasia to
organize your videos, right

00:06:26.599 --> 00:06:28.640
here under Create, you
can see the different ways

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:30.720
that you can make a
recording inside of Canvas.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:33.500
So if you want to
prerecord, you just

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:36.260
go to the Schedule Recording.

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:39.620
But I've also used it to
upload pre-done videos.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.999
Anyway, it's quick, smooth.

00:06:41.999 --> 00:06:43.790
Now I'll shut up, so
you can ask questions.

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:44.540
[LAUGHTER]

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:45.820
What have you got?

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:46.669
Yes?

00:06:46.669 --> 00:06:49.830
Another nice thing about this
is you can annotate time codes

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:52.940
to put in to, say, wake
up, pay attention here,

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:55.090
or this is the example I
did in class, or whatever.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.970
And the students can also send
questions, based on time codes.

00:06:57.970 --> 00:06:58.810
Yeah, which is cool.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:02.270
And partly, because they
have these slides as well,

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:04.574
they can always just slide
along here and see what's

00:07:04.574 --> 00:07:05.740
the slide number they're on.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.840
So a lot of them will have a
hard copy in front of them,

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.160
even as they're watching
the videos to make notes on.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.841
Other questions?

00:07:12.841 --> 00:07:13.340
Yes?

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:15.256
You mentioned at the
beginning of the semester

00:07:15.256 --> 00:07:17.461
you set it out to record.

00:07:17.461 --> 00:07:17.960
Correct

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:20.970
So you [INAUDIBLE] the recording
yourself, using Panopto.

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:21.470
Right.

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:24.122
So how did it talk to the
box that you all used?

00:07:24.122 --> 00:07:25.330
You can talk to John Harford.

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:26.090
He'll tell you all about it.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:28.048
But literally, the way
it works, I'll show you.

00:07:28.048 --> 00:07:30.354
If I were to go and schedule
a recording quickly here,

00:07:30.354 --> 00:07:32.270
it says, I'm going to
go schedule a recording.

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:35.540
And they know where I teach,
so they've given me access

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:36.710
to a couple of rooms.

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:39.830
And so I just say, in this room,
at this time, on these days,

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:40.749
turn on.

00:07:40.749 --> 00:07:41.747
OK.

00:07:41.747 --> 00:07:43.743
That's how it works.

00:07:43.743 --> 00:07:45.240
Other questions?

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:45.741
Yes?

00:07:45.741 --> 00:07:47.198
Do you tell the
students explicitly

00:07:47.198 --> 00:07:49.110
that you're going to be
filming your classes?

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:49.609
I do.

00:07:49.609 --> 00:07:52.284
And do you find that has any
impact on their willingness

00:07:52.284 --> 00:07:53.650
to ask you questions?

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:54.666
It has not.

00:07:54.666 --> 00:07:57.040
The particular groups that I
teach, after a class or two,

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:58.665
they learn I'm pretty
low key, and they

00:07:58.665 --> 00:08:00.640
ask questions no matter what.

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:02.920
And the camera certainly
isn't looking at them.

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:04.550
And in some ways,
the questions--

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:07.690
one thing I had to learn
was, the questions don't--

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:09.160
the mic doesn't pick them up.

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:11.800
So if they say something that
I'll be embarrassed for them,

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:12.850
I don't repeat what they said.

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:13.933
And no one will ever know.

00:08:13.933 --> 00:08:14.530
[LAUGHTER]

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:17.247
But I tell them on day one, you
will be recorded in this class.

00:08:17.247 --> 00:08:19.080
And you can use this
class however you want.

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.230
But I didn't hear
anybody saying,

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:22.300
I don't feel comfortable
being recorded here.

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:24.320
It hasn't come up.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:24.820
Yes?

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:27.236
Have you noticed any difference
in the student performance

00:08:27.236 --> 00:08:30.539
for that 25% or that 40%
who never come to class?

00:08:30.539 --> 00:08:33.080
I don't have enough data to say
anything relevant about that.

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:35.131
But what I would say is,
the last, last thing--

00:08:35.131 --> 00:08:36.130
I know I'm out of time--

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:38.463
I'm going to show you, is
that for any particular video,

00:08:38.463 --> 00:08:41.440
you can go get all the stats
for that particular video.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:42.940
And part of what's
interesting is

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:46.300
to see just the distribution
of who watched it when.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:50.022
So for this one here, I'm going
to set it so it goes over the--

00:08:50.022 --> 00:08:50.980
Are those the accounts?

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:55.060
Or do you have it
tied to their net ID?

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:56.840
Canvas automatically
links them in,

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:59.600
so it's sort of set
up automatically.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.660
Anyway, what you can
do here is that, I can

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:03.243
actually-- it's not
[INAUDIBLE], but I

00:09:03.243 --> 00:09:05.320
can see exactly who
watches the video when.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:06.560
Now, the video went up here.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.680
So these are the people who
got right on it and watched it.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:09.520
These are the people
who waited until there

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:11.560
was a homework assignment
on that particular thing.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:13.010
And these are the people
who wanted to review,

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:15.040
because they needed it
for their final project.

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:17.074
And if you look at
usage by individual,

00:09:17.074 --> 00:09:19.240
you can see there are some
people who-- they're just

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:20.560
learners, they need extra time.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.390
And so they'll watch
it two or three times.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:23.660
Then, there's the
people who sit down,

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:25.180
and they watch it
once at a stretch.

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:27.730
But there's also
plenty of people who--

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:29.360
like they want 10
minutes at a time.

